# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the code is
#   intended to run in multiple environments; otherwise, check them in:
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1256, Checkpipfile.lock into git because it is used for
#   reproducible builds.
#   However, in case of a library, you should not check it in:
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock contains the resolved dependencies,
#   and should be checked-in if you build a runnable application.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock contains the resolved dependencies,
#   and should be checked-in if you build a runnable application.
# pdm.lock

# PEP 582; project local packages directory (used by pdm)
__pypackages__/

